# L §5.16 Decisions and projections: a query around a read, "mean(…) or quantile(…, q), computed in closed form";
# "A query that has no closed form ... stands only in an ask line ... (LOAD-ASKONLY elsewhere)", so one the Closed
# forms table gives stands in a rule. g = uniform(0, 1): mean (a + b)/2 = 0.5, exact (table); share(g < lo) with
# lo = 1 is cdf(D, 1) = 1, at the support's upper end exactly 1. quantile of a distribution value (L §5.16
# The closed list: "Called on a distribution value, ... and quantile(d, q) are these functions, in a def as in an
# ask"): uniform(1, 3)'s type-1 50 % quantile is the smallest x with cdf(x) >= 0.5, 2. (Its mean, md, ask b, is gone:
# "mean(d) of a distribution value is refused", round 18 C1-47, L5_16_mean_of_dist_value.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input g: dist
input lo: num
input hi: num
input q: num
def mq: num = mean(g) at reader
def qd: num = quantile(uniform(lo, hi) to 0.01, q) at reader
def sq: num = share(g < lo) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  g = uniform(0, 1) to 0.01
  lo = 1 "s"
  hi = 3 "s"
  q = 0.5 "s"

ask a: mq law 2026-06-30
ask c: qd law 2026-06-30
ask d: sq law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: 0.5
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
c: 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
d: 1
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
